From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:37:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 455/488] [DS4.1] Logprob top-k ids in TileLang; custom ids
 without torch glue

- compute_topk_scores' torch.topk (both paths) is one TileLang kernel:
  PyTorch 2.13's order (radix keys, NaN first, ties to the lower column,
  then the k <= 32 bitonic network's tie order), k up to 32. A larger
  --max-logprobs, or -1, is refused at startup; no torch.topk path.
- The custom-ids fill writes every column (0 and invalid where unused),
  so its outputs are allocated empty, and the log-softmax writes -inf in
  invalid columns in its own store (the zeros and masked_fill gone).
- Top-k ids refuse logits without a unit column stride (no copy path).
